                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I thoroughly enjoyed Northern Tale and would play it again! \nhttps://steamcommunity.com/id/TopazMystique/recommended/417410 \n\nHowever, Northern Tale 2 is a different matter even though it does cater to my playing style. Rather than rushing through trying to complete each level in a certain amount of time, I like to play relaxed and complete everything: all resources picked up, all potholes in the roads filled, all buildings leveled up to the max, etc. Northern Tale 2 allows me to do that most of the time and doesn't penalize me for playing that way (3 stars awarded on all completed levels). There were a few of the later levels that I did just the bare minimum to complete the level because of the aggravating roots and ladders (see below).\n\nWhat I disliked most about it is the obnoxious requirements in later levels: the dragon (level 30) that kept setting fires, the ladders that slowed workers down (starting in level 31) and the roots (starting in level 33)! The roots are in almost every level after that and require food and gold to be able to remove the roots as they pop up in paths or cover buildings. Once the roots cover a building, no resources are produced until the roots are removed. \n\nOne good thing is that I only found one or two levels that had \"strategy meltdown\" (choosing the wrong strategy requiring a restart of the level) which was an improvement over Northern Tale, It is usually apparent relatively quickly so doesn't waste a lot of time replaying the level with a different strategy.\n\nIf you like the genre, you might want to give it a whirl. If you are new to time management / strategy, you might want to try Northern Tale instead. https://store.steampowered.com/app/417410/Northern_Tale/ Personally, I will NOT be playing Northern Tale 2 again!",
